{"id": "section-body-11741", "title": "Dysmenorrhea", "chapterId": "chapter-eleven", "tocLevel": 4, "tocPath": ["APPROACH TO PATIENTS WITH EMERGENCY CONDITIONS", "OBSTETRICS, GYNECOLOGY AND CONTRACEPTION", "Postpartum Care", "Dysmenorrhea"], "blocks": [{"id": "body-11741", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Dysmenorrhea", "runs": [{"text": "Dysmenorrhea"}], "level": 4, "list": {"level": 2, "numberingId": "1452"}}, {"id": "body-11742", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "It is a painful menstruation preventing normal activities and requires medication. There are 2 types of dysmenorrhea:", "runs": [{"text": "It"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "painful"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "menstruation"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "preventing"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "normal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "activities"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "requires"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "medication."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "There"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "are"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "2"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "types"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "dysmenorrhea:"}]}, {"id": "body-11744", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Primary (no organic cause). Typically, pain occurs on the first day of menses, usually about the time the flow begins, improves with age, shortly after menarche.", "runs": [{"text": "Primary", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "(no", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "organic", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "cause).", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "Typically,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "pain"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "occurs"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "on"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "first"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "day"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "menses,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "usually"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "about"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "time"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "flow"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "begins,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "improves with age, shortly after menarche."}]}, {"id": "body-11746", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Secondary (pathological cause) e.g., usually the pain is due to other underlying causes involving reproductive organs e.g., PID, endometriosis, etc. late on-set (72 hours and more) of menstrual cycle, low back pain", "runs": [{"text": "Secondary (pathological cause) ", "bold": true}, {"text": "e.g., usually the pain is due to other underlying causes involving reproductive organs e.g., PID, endometriosis, etc. late on-set (72 hours and more) of menstrual cycle, low back pain"}]}, {"id": "body-11749", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Pharmacological Treatment", "runs": [{"text": "Pharmacological"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Treatment"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-11750", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "A: ibuprofen (PO) 200–600mg 8hourly (maximum 2.4 g/day)", "runs": [{"text": "A:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "ibuprofen"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(PO)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "200–600mg"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "8hourly"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(maximum"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "2.4"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "g/day)"}]}, {"id": "body-11751", "type": "paragraph", "style": "Heading3", "text": "OR", "runs": [{"text": "OR"}], "level": 3, "conjunction": true}, {"id": "body-11752", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "A: acetylsalicylic acid (PO) 300–600mg 4hourly", "runs": [{"text": "A:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "acetylsalicylic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "acid"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(PO)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "300–600mg"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "4hourly"}]}, {"id": "body-11753", "type": "paragraph", "style": "Heading3", "text": "OR", "runs": [{"text": "OR"}], "level": 3, "conjunction": true}, {"id": "body-11754", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "C: diclofenac (PO) 50–100mg 8–12hourly", "runs": [{"text": "C:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "diclofenac"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(PO)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "50–100mg"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "8–12hourly"}]}, {"id": "body-11755", "type": "paragraph", "style": "Heading3", "text": "OR", "runs": [{"text": "OR"}], "level": 3, "conjunction": true}, {"id": "body-11756", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "B: mefenamic acid (PO) 500mg 8hourly", "runs": [{"text": "B:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "mefenamic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "acid"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(PO)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "500mg"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "8hourly"}]}, {"id": "body-11757", "type": "paragraph", "style": "Heading3", "text": "AND", "runs": [{"text": "AND"}], "level": 3, "conjunction": true}, {"id": "body-11758", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "A: hyoscine butyl bromide (PO) 20mg 8hourly for 5days", "runs": [{"text": "A:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "hyoscine"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "butyl"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "bromide"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(PO)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "20mg"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "8hourly"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "for"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "5days"}]}, {"id": "body-11759", "type": "paragraph", "style": "Heading3", "text": "AND", "runs": [{"text": "AND"}], "level": 3, "conjunction": true}, {"id": "body-11760", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "C: norethisterone 5mg (PO) 24 hourly to start on 5th day of cycle for 14 days for 3 cycles, 10mg 24 hourly to start on day 5 of cycle for 14 days for patient not responding well on small dose", "runs": [{"text": "C", "bold": true}, {"text": ": norethisterone 5mg (PO) 24 hourly to start on 5th day of cycle for 14 days for 3 cycles, 10mg 24 hourly to start on day 5 of cycle for 14 days for patient not responding well on small dose"}]}, {"id": "body-11761", "type": "paragraph", "style": "Heading3", "text": "OR", "runs": [{"text": "OR"}], "level": 3, "conjunction": true}, {"id": "body-11762", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "S: dydrogesterone 10mg (PO) 24 hourly to start on 5th day of cycle for 14 days for 3 cycles, 20mg 24 hourly to start on day 5 of cycle for 14 days for patient not responding well on small dose.", "runs": [{"text": "S: ", "bold": true}, {"text": "dydrogesterone 10mg (PO) 24 hourly to start on 5th day of cycle for 14 days for 3 cycles, 20mg 24 hourly to start on day 5 of cycle for 14 days for patient not responding well on small dose."}]}], "source": {"file": "medical.docx", "chapter": "Obstetrics, gynecology and contraception", "start": "body-11741", "end": "body-11762"}}